Quoting  Philip Potter  <pgp@doc.ic.ac.uk>:
>But when the same spell is cast by two characters with the same Int, 
>Wis, XL, skill and armor, why is the nonwizard better?

That was my first thought, but the answer is that the wizard isn't used to
wearing the armour. 

Imagine a fit and healthy hiker and an unfit office worker. The hiker can
walk further than the office worker. Now have them both do it in the
office worker's stiletto heels, which the hiker never wears. Even though
the hiker is better at walking, the equipment is so unfamiliar and
cumbersome that being used to it is more important that being used to the
activity.
